 html[dir="rtl"] .start-selling :where(h1, h2, h3, h4, p, li, button, a, span) {
   unicode-bidi: plaintext;
 }
+/* [scene-scope V1] The paused-scene rules used to match every descendant (`:where(*)`). A rule whose subject is
+   universal makes an attribute change on the scene restyle the whole subtree (WebKit AttributeChangeInvalidation /
+   StyleInvalidator, Blink "invalidates subtree"): 172-399 elements at every scene flip. The subject is now the
+   list of elements that can carry a CSS animation (the subject compound of every `animation`/`animation-name`
+   rule in this file and DialogHeader.css; pseudo-elements were never matched by `:where(*)`), so a flip restyles
+   only those. animation-play-state is not inherited, so an unlisted element only differs by keeping a CSS
+   animation running while its scene is paused (CPU, not a visual change). */
 .start-selling [data-start-selling-scene="paused"],
-.start-selling [data-start-selling-scene="paused"] :where(*) {
+.start-selling [data-start-selling-scene="paused"] .commission-underline,
